WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:06.279
Speaker 1: In other news, Mary Trump, niece
of former President Donald Trump, came out

00:00:06.279 --> 00:00:13.340
with a phenomenal article in The New Republic
recently where she basically, well, she psychoanalyzed

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:16.410
a lot of her uncle's administration.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:21.530
But there's one part that I want to hit on
more than others, and that is the part where

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:24.560
she talks about the big lie, right?

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:29.119
The big lie that the election was stolen,
which, as she points out, Donald Trump began

00:00:29.119 --> 00:00:34.219
telling that lie on November 7th, which was
the day that the 2020 election was officially

00:00:34.219 --> 00:00:37.530
called for Joe Biden.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:42.859
And on that very day, he started the Big Lie
and of course, he had all the horrible people

00:00:42.859 --> 00:00:45.629
whispering in his ear that, oh, here you got
to do this.

00:00:45.629 --> 00:00:47.510
Giuliani was there.

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:49.940
Mark Meadows was there.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:54.629
All these individuals, even some private lawyers
telling him, you've got to challenge this,

00:00:54.629 --> 00:00:58.449
you got to say it was fake.

00:00:58.449 --> 00:01:02.679
And Mary Trump says that the reason her uncle
did this.

00:01:02.679 --> 00:01:12.860
Is because he was absolutely humiliated, humiliated
by the fact that he lost the presidential

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:17.110
election to Joe Biden.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:19.170
All this was.

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:24.850
Was his hubris not allowing him to accept
the fact that he lost to somebody like Joe

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:28.060
Biden?

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:35.570
And so he had to, as a defense mechanism for
himself, create this alternative timeline,

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:38.450
this alternative reality.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:40.730
We're in his head.

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:45.010
He actually won the election because of all
the fraud.

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:50.230
So we had the election challenges, we've had
the recounts, we've had to go through and

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:53.890
recertify, we've had the signature match,
we now have the ballot audits.

00:01:53.890 --> 00:02:02.780
And all of it, she points out, is this defense
mechanism to protect his bruised ego.

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:07.590
The humiliation that he still feels to this
day.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:12.870
For losing that election.

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:19.260
But the problem is his delusion, his defense
mechanism is not just limited to him now.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:24.620
It is in psychological terms, a shared psychosis
now.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:31.819
Right, it has seemingly infected millions
of others who have now been sucked into the

00:02:31.819 --> 00:02:35.739
delusion to believe that the 2020 election
was stolen.

00:02:35.739 --> 00:02:40.060
I mean, how many polls have we seen just over
the last two months showing a majority of

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:45.010
Republicans now think the election was stolen?

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:46.279
That's a terrifying thought.

00:02:46.279 --> 00:02:50.689
I haven't seen any polls in the last couple
of weeks, so maybe that number has changed,

00:02:50.689 --> 00:02:55.440
maybe it's going back down and you don't have
a majority of Republicans thinking that anymore.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:59.830
But the fact that we ever did that, we ever
even hit 60 percent of Republicans saying

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:04.379
this is terrifying because there was never
any fraud.

00:03:04.379 --> 00:03:11.719
In fact, the few cases of fraud that we found,
the individual cases all appear to be Trump

00:03:11.719 --> 00:03:12.719
supporters.

00:03:12.719 --> 00:03:18.060
That's what we're living with, but they still
can't accept it because he won't accept it

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:20.420
and he'll never accept it.

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:25.639
To the day he dies, Donald Trump, every time
he gets in front of a camera or he gets a

00:03:25.639 --> 00:03:30.389
microphone, is going to remind us that he
thinks the 2020 election was stolen.

00:03:30.389 --> 00:03:32.799
He has done that this year.

00:03:32.799 --> 00:03:40.099
Every time he gets on stage, every time he
has an audience, he says the same thing.

00:03:40.099 --> 00:03:44.010
Even though the ballot audits have produced
no fraud, even though the recounts have produced

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:50.510
no fraud, even though the lawsuits have produced
no fraud, even though the cyber symposium

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:54.590
produced no hacking evidence at all, no fraud.

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:57.560
He'll never stop.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:02.989
And Mary, Trump's explanation of this really
lays it all bare.

00:04:02.989 --> 00:04:08.560
He won't stop because he can't stop because
his narcissism simply won't let him.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:13.390
I am Ferren Cousins in for David Pakman, we'll
be right back with more of The David Pakman

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:13.719
Show

